QuestGuidance.Register("en",41,{
[1281]="700097D5\n1\tCollect Small Statue Piece (total: 12)\030Collect Large Statue Piece (total: 4)\tTomb-robbers in Tyrn Fornech may be carrying small statue pieces, and larger pieces can likely be found in their camp on Rantost, the island west of Ost Forod. Robin Dunkley has been inspired by the broken statuary you recovered with the dream of remaking the complete statue and wants you to recover the pieces of it.\n2\tBring statue pieces to Robin Dunkley\tRobin Dunkley is at Ost Forod, east of Rantost, in Tyrn Fornech in Evendim. You have recovered many pieces of statuary, and now you should bring them to Robin Dunkley to see if they belong to the statue he seeks to repair.\n",
[1282]="70045452\n1\tCollect ward pieces (total: 6)\tWard pieces can be found near Púkel-men statues in the Drúadan Forest. You should collect ward pieces for the Woses.\n2\tBring the ward pieces to Ghâr-buri-Bhâm\tGhâr-buri-Bhâm is in Drû Bhûta. You should bring the ward pieces to Ghâr-buri-Bhâm so that he can craft a new ward for the village.\n3\tWait for Ghâr-buri-Bhâm to craft the ward\tGhâr-buri-Bhâm is in Drû Bhûta. You should wait for Ghâr-buri-Bhâm to craft the ward.\n4\tSpeak with Ghâr-buri-Bhâm\tGhâr-buri-Bhâm is in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with Ghâr-buri-Bhâm about the ward.\n5\tSpeak with Ghân-buri-Ghân\tGhân-buri-Ghân can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with Ghân-buri-Ghân.\n",
[1283]="7006B07A\n1\tSpeak with Khôltekh on the dock\tSpeak with Khôltekh on the dock.\n2\tMove to stop Sêkhta from commandeering The Candle of Umbar\tMove to stop Sêkhta and his men from commandeering The Candle of Umbar.\n3\tDefeat Sêkhta's guards (total: 3)\tDefeat Sêkhta's guards!\n4\tDefeat Sêkhta's honour guard\tDefeat Sêkhta's honour guard!\n5\tDefeat Sêkhta's honour guard\tDefeat Sêkhta's honour guard!\n6\tListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta\tListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta.\n7\tListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta\tListen to Khôltekh confront Sêkhta.\n8\tSpeak with Khôltekh on the dock\tSpeak with Khôltekh on the dock.\n",
[1284]="70072F05\n1\tExamine the banner in view of the Orc ship and the Heirsworn ship\tStanding by a banner in view of a black-sailed Orc ship and an orange-sailed Heirsworn ship, you consider a means of turning the two crews against each other.\n2\tDefeat Orc ship-mates on the black-sailed ship (total: 4)\030Defeat Heirsworn ship-mates on the orange-sailed ship (total: 4)\tYou decide to defeat Orcs on the black-sailed ship and Heirsworn Corsairs on the orange-sailed ship, turning them against each other.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have wrought confusion among the ships of the Heirsworn and the Orcs.\n",
[1285]="7002D414\n1\tDestroy food-stores in Gazatmur (total: 10)\tGoblin food-stores can likely be found in Gazatmur in the eastern Great Delving. You should destroy food-stores in Gazatmur to dismantle this camp as an established keep for the enemy.\n2\tReturn to Wigfast\tWigfast is perched just beyond Gazatmur in the Great Delving. You should return to Wigfast.\n",
[1286]="70019D2C\n1\tPatrol the banks of the Anduin (0/4)\tThe river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien. Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.\n2\tPatrol the banks of the Anduin (1/4)\tThe river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien. Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.\n3\tPatrol the banks of the Anduin (2/4)\tThe river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien. Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.\n4\tPatrol the banks of the Anduin (3/4)\tThe river Anduin runs northwards from the Vineyards of Lórien. Farasdúr has asked you to patrol the banks of the Anduin and ensure that no enemy forces have gained a purchase on the west side of the river.\n5\tTalk to Farasdúr near the Vineyards of Lothlórien\tFarasdúr is near the Vineyards of Lórien, south of the Anduin. You should return to Farasdúr and tell him the results of your patrol.\n",
[1287]="70052B27\n1\tCollect fish from nets along the Anduin (total: 8)\tNets can be found along the eastern shores of the Anduin in Woodsedge. Germund has asked you to gather fish from nets along the Anduin.\n2\tDeliver the fish to Germund in Hultvís\tGermund can be found in Hultvís. You have gathered a number of fish and should now deliver them to Germund.\n",
[1288]="70054809\n1\tDefeat foes at Angathrai\tAngathrai can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat foes at Angathrai.\n2\tDefeat shades at Angathrai (total: 12)\030Defeat fell summoners at Angathrai (total: 3)\tAngathrai can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat foes at Angathrai.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many foes at Angathrai.\n",
[1289]="7005480A\n1\tDestroy cursed runes at Angathrai\tAngathrai can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy cursed runes at Angathrai.\n2\tDestroy cursed runes at Angathrai (total: 14)\tAngathrai can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy cursed runes at Angathrai.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroy many cursed runes at Angathrai.\n",
[1290]="7004A383\n1\tSearch for more such stones and try to determine their purpose within Anglach in Udûn.\t\n2\tFind a use for the strange stones\tTry to determine the strange stones' purpose within Anglach in Udûn.\n3\tDefeat Gúrflak the fire grim\tThe door you opened held a great fire grim within it!\n4\tCompleted\tDefeated Gúrflak the ancient fire grim.\n",
[1291]="7004A38A\n1\tCollect artifacts of the Last Alliance (total: 10)\tYou should gather artifacts of the Last Alliance within Anglach in Udûn.\n2\tBring the artifacts to the Foothold\tYou should bring the artifacts you gathered in Anglach to the Foothold Camp in Udûn.\n",
[1292]="7004A399\n1\tDefeat Forge-worker Orcs in Anglach (total: 6)\030Defeat forge-worker slaves in Anglach (total: 6)\tYou should defeat slave and Orc-Forgeworkers in the depths of Anglach in Udûn.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many forge-workers in the depths of Anglach.\n",
[1293]="7004B597\n1\tDefeat Ongdrágh, Master of the Mines\tOngdrágh, Master of the Mines can be found deep within Anglach. You should defeat Ongdrágh, Master of the Mines.\n2\tTalk to Candúr\tCandúr can be found at the Udûn Foothold. You should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[1294]="7000C09A\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Council of the North.\n",
[1295]="7000C09B\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Council of the North.\n",
[1296]="7000C09C\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Council of the North.\n",
[1297]="7000C09D\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred of the Council of the North.\n",
[1298]="700698B0\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
[1299]="700647D2\n1\tTalk to Nekhtan at Bail Avarc\tNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. Soltakh has asked you to speak to Nekhtan about the recent rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Nekhtan.\n2\tTalk to Nekhtan and hear his tale of the rite of Clúcath\tNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. Nekhtan has offered to tell you the tale of the rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Nekhtan and hear his account.\n3\tTalk to Nekhtan at Bail Avarc\tNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. Nekhtan has told you to tale of the rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Nekhtan.\n4\tHear what Nekhtan knows of Crannog's fate\tNekhtan has offered to tell you what he knows of Crannog's fate after his defeat at Clúcath.\n5\tTalk to Nekhtan at Bail Avarc\tNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. Nekhtan has told you to tale of the fate that befell Crannog and the Trév Gállorg after the Iron Crown returned to Carn Dûm. You should talk to Nekhtan.\n6\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. After informing you that Crannog was taken by the Iron Crown, Nekhtan has suggested that Soltakh might know of secret ways into the city of Carn Dûm. You should return to Soltakh.\n",
[1300]="700647D6\n1\tHelp Rhúnelleth with 'Into Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens'\030Help Indagir with 'Remedies for Maladies'\tRhúnelleth and Indagir can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Soltakh has asked you to aid Rhúnelleth and Indagir in their efforts at Sant Lhoer and Thaurisgar as it will advance the fight against the Iron Crown in Carn Dûm. You should help Rhúnelleth and Indagir.\n2\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have helped Rhúnelleth and Indagir with their tasks at Sant Lhoer and Thaurisgar—for better and worse. You should return to Bail Avarc and talk to Soltakh.\n3\tTalk to Lágsaith and listen to her tale of 'The Lair of Vermin'\tLágsaith can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Soltakh has heard word that a company of Trév Duvárdain battled against the Iron Crown in the sewers of Carn Dûm. You should talk to Lágsaith and learn of what has happened.\n4\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have heard Lágsaith's tale of the Trév Duvárdain's fight against the Iron Crown in Sagroth. You should talk to Soltakh.\n5\tTalk to Finrúth at Bail Avarc\tFinrúth can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Soltakh has asked you to speak to a woman of the Trév Duvárdain named Finrúth, who came to Bail Avarc seeking shelter from the Iron Crown. You should talk to Finrúth.\n",
[1301]="700647D5\n1\tCollect a hearty meal for Finrúth\030Collect a waterskin for Finrúth\tA hearty meal and a waterskin can be found at Bail Avarc. Before Finrúth recounts the tale of how she came to turn on the Iron Crown, she has asked for water and a meal. You should collect a hearty meal and a waterskin for Finrúth.\n2\tDeliver the hearty meal and waterskin to Finrúth\tFinrúth can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have collected a hearty meal and a waterskin for Finrúth. You should return to Finrúth.\n3\tTalk to Finrúth\tFinrúth can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Finrúth has offered to tell you the tale of how she came to abandon the Iron Crown and the true nature of the \"bódraillan\" that now dwell in Carn Dûm. You should talk to Finrúth.\n4\tTalk to Finrúth at Bail Avarc\tFinrúth can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Finrúth has told you the tale of how she came to abandon the Iron Crown and you now know the true nature of the \"bódraillan\" that now dwell in Carn Dûm. You should talk to Finrúth.\n5\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have listened to Finrúth's tale of the shard of Tauressar's power and learned that Crannog may still live within Carn Dûm. You should talk to Soltakh.\n",
[1302]="700647D4\n1\tTalk to Nekhtan at Bail Avarc\tNekhtan can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Soltakh has told you to prepare to set siege to Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel. You should talk to Nekhtan and inform him that Crannog still lives before you set out.\n2\tTravel to Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel\tGwathrenost, the citadel of the Witch-king of Angmar can be found at the heart of Carn Dûm. You should travel to Gwathrenost and put an end to the Iron Crown's plot to use the shard of Tauressar against the free-folk of the North. NOTE: You can advance this quest on any difficulty Tier of the Raid: 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel'.\n3\tFind Crannog in Gwathrenost\tCrannog can be found somewhere high in Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel. You must continue your search for Crannog as you battle the Iron Crown at Gwathrenost.\n4\tTalk to Crannog at Gwathrenost\tCrannog can be found high in Gwathrenost. You have found Crannog alive, but severely mistreated by the Iron Crown. You should speak to Crannog.\n5\tTalk to Soltakh at Gwathrenost\tSoltakh can be found in Gwathrenost. After fighting through Gwathrenost, you have found Crannog—alive, but in poor health. You should talk to Soltakh.\n6\tDestroy the shard of Tauressar\tThe Shard of Tauressar can be found in Tham Mornarcham, the highest chamber within Gwathrenost. You must defeat High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd. You must also destroy the shard of Tauressar that its fell power can no longer bend the wills of the free-folk of the North.\n7\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have triumphed over the Iron Crown, defeating High Priestess Ásachal and High Chieftain Claghórd and destroying the shard of Tauressar. You should return to Bail Avarc and talk to Soltakh.\n8\tTalk to Crannog at Bail Avarc\tCrannog can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. You have rescued Crannog from the Iron Crown and he has been safely escorted back to Bail Avarc. You should talk to Crannog.\n",
[1303]="700647D3\n1\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog can be found at Bail Avarc in the foothills of the Ephel Angren in Angmar. Crannog has asked you to accompany him and the Trév Gállorg to Fail-á-Khro where he hopes to parley with the Trév Duvárdain. You should talk to Crannog when you are ready to set out.\n2\tMeet Crannog and Soltakh at the outskirts of Aughaire\tCrannog and Soltakh can be found at the outskirts of Aughaire in Angmar. After the parley at Fail-á-Khro, Crannog and the Trév Gállorg have returned to Aughaire. You should meet Crannog and Soltakh at Aughaire.\n3\tTalk to Soltakh at the outskirts of Aughaire\tSoltakh can be found on the outskirts of Aughaire in Angmar. After the parley at Fail-á-Khro, Crannog and the Trév Gállorg have returned to Aughaire. You should talk to Soltakh.\n4\tTalk to Crannog at the outskirts of Aughaire\tCrannog can be found on the outskirts of Aughaire in Angmar. After the parley at Fail-á-Khro, Crannog and the Trév Gállorg have returned to Aughaire. You should talk to Crannog.\n",
[1304]="7006443C\n1\tTravel to Bail Avarc in Angmar\tBail Avarc can be found in Angmar, south-east of Carn Dûm. Crannog has sent you a missive requesting your aid at Bail Avarc in Angmar. You should travel to Bail Avarc. NOTE: Bail Avarc can initially only be accessed via stable-master routes. Bail Avarc can be reached via the Stable-masters at Esteldín, Gath Forthnír, and the stables of Rivendell.\n2\tFind Crannog at Bail Avarc\tCrannog can be found at Bail Avarc. You have arrived at Bail Avarc and should seek out Crannog. NOTE: Bail Avarc can initially only be accessed via stable-master routes. Bail Avarc can be reached via the stable-masters at Esteldín, Gath Forthnír, and the stables of Rivendell.\n3\tTalk to Soltakh at Bail Avarc\tSoltakh can be found at Bail Avarc. You have arrived at Bail Avarc. You have not yet found Crannog, but Soltakh wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Soltakh. NOTE: Bail Avarc can initially only be accessed via stable-master routes. Bail Avarc can be reached via the stable-masters at Esteldín, Gath Forthnír, and the stables of Rivendell.\n",
[1305]="70025B6D\n1\tBring the Satchel to Gúrhebnir\tThe Rangers are at Tinnudir, south-west of Tham Ornen. One of the Rangers will be eager to examine the satchel and determine what its contents mean.\n",
[1306]="700088F2\n1\tReturn Chieftain's seals to First Marshal Sathryth\030Collect Chieftain's seal\tThe Chieftains of Angmar may be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors. Chieftains amongst Angmar's army bear seals that denote their station. Slay them and take their seals to earn recognition amongst the Free Peoples. First Marshal Sathryth has promised a reward for the seals you bring her.\n",
[1307]="7000B100\n1\tTalk to Gelbes at Glân Vraig\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. The Rangers will assist in retaking Tírith Rhaw, but they request that you take the place of a Ranger in Eriador while they remain to the Ettenmoors to fight in your stead. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Gelbes\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. A Ranger came to the Ettenmoors in your stead and fought valiantly while you patrolled Eriador in his stead. You should speak with Gelbes.\n",
[1308]="7000B0FE\n1\tTalk to Gelbes at Glân Vraig\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. The Rangers will assist in retaking the Isendeep, but they request that you take the place of a Ranger in Eriador, while they come to the Ettenmoors to fight in your stead. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Gelbes\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. A Ranger came to the Ettenmoors in your stead and fought valiantly, while you patrolled Eriador in his stead.\n",
[1309]="70000CBB\n1\tDefeat Gaunt Protector (total: 3)\tThe gaunt-men protectors who command the wights might be lurking in the ruins in the south-western reaches of Agamaur. Prove your valour to Eriac. He has set you the task of dealing with the gaunt-men who lead Ivar's wights in the hopes that the curses binding the wights might be broken.\n2\tTalk to Eriac the Strong\tEriac awaits you at the Eglain camp in the southern reaches of Agamaur. Eriac set you to the task of killing the gaunt-men protectors, a task to which you proved equal. You should return to Eriac with your report.\n",
[1310]="700088F3\n1\tReturn tracker's badges to First Marshal Sathryth\030Collect tracker's badges (total: 10)\tTrackers can be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors. Forces in the service to Angmar may each carry a seal of their station. Search among the enemy for these badges. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised a reward for the badges you bring her.\n",
[1311]="700088F4\n1\tReturn soldier's patches to First Marshal Sathryth\030Collect soldier's patches (total: 5)\tSoldiers in the service to Angmar may each carry a seal of their station. Search among the enemy for these badges. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised to reward you for the patches you bring her.\n",
[1312]="700088F5\n1\tReturn taskmaster's honourifics to First Marshal Sathryth\030Collect taskmaster's honourifics (total: 5)\tThe taskmasters of Angmar can be found among the Enemy in the Ettenmoors. The taskmasters who drive the Angmarim war-host into a frenzy bear honourifics of their station. Collect these to earn commendation from the Army of the Free Peoples. First Marshal Sathryth at Ost Ringdyr has promised to reward you for the taskmaster's honourifics you bring her.\n",
})
